{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"1d9558e67f6208a169ce6acd04bdf141a6935ce62d0392cd8c1dc20cca32b880","digest":{"component_or_area":"test design guidance and standards","key_entities":["examples/agent-skills/shared/test-design.md","examples/agent-skills/rebar-debug/test-design.md","examples/agent-skills/rebar-implement/test-design.md","examples/agent-skills/rebar-brainstorm/test-design.md","tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/mutate/test_outbound_comment_length_convergence.py","tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_comment_dedup_key_matches_send_fit.py","tests/unit/test_skill_shared_sync.py","comment_limits.truncate_comment_body","AdfCodec.fit_outbound","acli_cli_ops.add_comment"],"problem_keywords":["convergence test","test oracle","re-derived model","external effect","send path","stale assertion","test design"],"propositions":["Convergence tests that re-derive the external-effect side using the same helpers as the code under test stay green when the actual implementation drifts, missing their only intended failure mode.","The oracle for a convergence assertion must be captured from a real call site with only irreducible boundaries stubbed, never recomposed from the helper functions that the call site uses.","The rule distinguishing defective re-derived oracles from sanctioned characterization tests is intent-based (whether one side represents an external effect), not syntactically detectable, making automated lint infeasible.","Documentation guidance on convergence test design must be recorded in the shared test-design standard and kept byte-identical across all consuming skill directories."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c